.TH RCAL 1 "September 2026" "rcal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rcal \- CLI calendar tool with CalDAV synchronization
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rcal
.RI [ COMMAND ] [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rcal
is a command-line calendar tool. It keeps an offline SQLite cache of your
events, displays day, week and month views, imports iCal (.ics) files, and
synchronizes bidirectionally with a CalDAV server (for example Radicale,
DAViCal, or Nextcloud Calendar).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B today
Show today's events.
.TP
.B week
Show an overview of the week containing the given date, or the current week.
.TP
.RS
.IP "\fB\-d, \-\-date\fR \fIDATE\fR"
Start date (\fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR); defaults to the current week.
.RE
.TP
.B month
Show an overview of the given month, or the current month.
.TP
.RS
.IP "\fB\-m, \-\-month\fR \fIMONTH\fR"
Month (\fIYYYY\-MM\fR); defaults to the current month.
.RE
.TP
.B show
Show events for a specific date.
.TP
.RS
.IP "\fBDATE\fR"
Date to show (\fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR).
.RE
.TP
.B import
Import an iCal (.ics) file. Interactively previews each event before adding;
a report is shown after the import.
.TP
.RS
.IP "\fBFILE\fR"
Path to the .ics file.
.IP "\fB\-\-add\fR"
Add all events without interactive prompts.
.IP "\fB\-\-dry-run\fR"
Preview only; do not modify the database.
.RE
.TP
.B sync
Synchronize with the CalDAV server configured in the config file. Discovers
calendars, pulls changes (adds, updates, deletions), and pushes locally
created events with an HTTP PUT. Prints per-calendar and total counts of
added, updated, unchanged, deleted and pushed events.
.TP
.B new
Create a new event. When run interactively (a TTY), missing values are
prompted for. When run non-interactively, \fB\-\-title\fR is required and
defaults are used for everything else.
.TP
.RS
.IP "\fB\-t, \-\-title\fR \fITITLE\fR"
Event title.
.IP "\fB\-d, \-\-date\fR \fIDATE\fR"
Event date (\fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR); defaults to today.
.IP "\fB\-\-time\fR \fITIME\fR"
Start time (24h \fIHH:MM\fR); defaults to 09:00.
.IP "\fB\-D, \-\-duration\fR \fIMINUTES\fR"
Duration in minutes; defaults to 60.
.IP "\fB\-a, \-\-all-day\fR"
Create an all-day event.
.IP "\fB\-l, \-\-location\fR \fILOCATION\fR"
Event location.
.IP "\fB\-\-description\fR \fIDESCRIPTION\fR"
Event description.
.IP "\fB\-c, \-\-calendar\fR \fICALENDAR\fR"
Target calendar (name or URL as shown by the \fBcalendars\fR command).
.RE
.TP
.B search
Search events by text. Matches the summary, description and location
(case-insensitive).
.TP
.RS
.IP "\fBQUERY\fR"
Search query.
.IP "\fB\-\-from\fR \fIDATE\fR"
Lower bound of the date range (\fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR).
.IP "\fB\-\-to\fR \fIDATE\fR"
Upper bound of the date range (\fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR).
.RE
.TP
.B calendars
List available calendars with their color swatches and event counts.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B rcal
reads a TOML configuration file. By default it looks in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rcal/config.toml
or (when that variable is unset)
.IR ~/.config/rcal/config.toml .
A config file is required for \fBsync\fR; create it manually if it does not
exist.
.PP
.nf
[server]
url = "https://dav.example.com/"
username = "alice"
password_command = "pass show caldav/alice"

[display]
default_view = "today"
time_format = "24h"
color_scheme = "auto"

[calendars]
show = []
hide = []

[notifications]
enabled = true
reminder_minutes = [15, 5]
.fi
.PP
The \fBdisplay\fR, \fBcalendars\fR and \fBnotifications\fR tables are
optional and their values fall back to the defaults shown above.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RCAL_PASSWORD
Password used for CalDAV authentication, used when
.B password_command
is not configured. The password is resolved in this order: the
.I password_command
from the config file, then the \fBRCAL_PASSWORD\fR environment variable, then
an interactive prompt. Passwords are never stored in the database.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the base directory for the config file.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Overrides the base directory for the database.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rcal/config.toml
Configuration file (see CONFIGURATION).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rcal/rcal.db
SQLite database holding the offline event cache and sync metadata
(etags, calendar associations).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Show today's events:
.nf
$ rcal today
.fi
.PP
Show the events of March 1, 2026:
.nf
$ rcal show 2026-03-01
.fi
.PP
Preview an iCal file without importing and then import everything:
.nf
$ rcal import schedule.ics --dry-run
$ rcal import schedule.ics --add
.fi
.PP
Create a one-hour meeting on a specific calendar:
.nf
$ rcal new --title "Design review" --date 2026-03-02 --time 14:00 \\
           --location "Room 3" --calendar "http://dav.example.com/alice/work/"
.fi
.PP
Synchronize with the CalDAV server:
.nf
$ rcal sync
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exit status is \fB0\fR on success and \fB1\fR on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR radicale (5),
.br
RFC 5545 (Internet Calendaring and Scheduling Core Object Specification)